remstart
    THE ACHIEVEMENTS
    the achievements of the game, on Steam. they are set up in Steamworks, where each has an API name, like
    END_REEF, and that name is all that the game knows of it: the titles, the words, the icons, and every
    language of them, are in Steamworks, and not in the strings of the game. fish_routines_achieve has the rest.

    THE ENDINGS. one for each of the six. END_HOME, END_REEF, END_ANCIENT, END_DIVER, END_NEPTUNE, and END_AVA,
    which is for getting through the last of her boards, when she is out of ideas.
    THE CARDS OF THE FAST. CARD_ROTATE and CARD_OATH, when the card is taken. see THE FAST in fish_headers_fast.
    ALL_QUESTS. every quest has been finished, in one game or another. QUEST_EVER_DONE keeps which have.
    THE RADIO. one for what every word does, so SING and SONG share one, and so do HELP and INFO. TUNA has
    none, because it turns debug mode on. FRIEND has its own, when it brings her back after she has gone.
    THE STATS. two numbers that Steam keeps, and that Steamworks unlocks the achievements of on its own when
    they get far enough: fish_popped (POP_1K, POP_10K, POP_100K) and games_finished (GAMES_10, GAMES_50,
    GAMES_100). a game is finished when it gets to the end of a game, whichever way, and not when it is left.
    the stats only reach Steam when they are stored, which is done at every upgrade screen and the end of a game.

    WHAT DOES NOT COUNT. a demo, a game that has had debug mode on, and a game started with one of the environment
    variables that are only for working on the game (isDebugEnvSet). the tests have no Steam at all.
    without Steam every one of the commands does nothing, so none of this needs to check for it.
remend

global ACHIEVE_ENV_DEBUG = 0 `1 when the game was started with an environment variable that is only for working on it. setup_achieve looks, once.
global ACHIEVE_POPPED = 0 `fish that have popped since the last were added to fish_popped. handle_combos counts them.
global dim ACHIEVE_MORSE$(24) `the achievement of every word of the radio, by the number of the word, or "" for none
